# Ignore everything
**

# Re-include only what is needed for an editable install of the package
# Nothing else is needed in the image.

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md

!qatrack/
!qatrack/**

!manage.py

# The default fixtures: QA categories, statuses, frequencies and tolerances,
# service types, areas and statuses, unit vendors, classes and types. Both
# install guides document `loaddata fixtures/defaults/*/*` as an install step
# (linux.rst, win.rst), and `manage.py generate_sample_data` loads them too.
# Excluded by the `**` above they were absent from the image, so neither could
# be done from a container: a Docker install started with no defaults at all
# and no way to add them.
!fixtures/
!fixtures/**

# Docker deployment files
!deploy/
!deploy/docker/
!deploy/docker/**

# Re-ignore sensitive files that could exist in an already-included path.

# Environment files
**/.env
**/*.env
**/*env.bak
**/*env.old

# Django secret key, user-data
**/secret_key.txt
**/user-data
**/user_data

# SSL certificates and private keys
**/certs
**/SSL
**/ssl
**/*.certificate
**/*.crt
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt.key

# potential DB backups
**/backups
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
